# Meta Rules - Rule Interpretation Guide

## Rule Priority (highest to lowest)
1. Security rules (never bypass)
2. Project-specific patterns
3. Tech stack conventions
4. General best practices

## When Rules Conflict
- Specific rules override general rules
- File-scoped rules override global rules
- Explicit instructions in chat override rules

## Default Behaviors
When no rule matches:
- Follow existing patterns in the file
- Check similar files in the codebase for conventions
- Ask for clarification on architectural decisions

## Rule Application
- Read the FULL rule before generating code
- Apply ALL relevant rules, not just the first match
- When uncertain, prefer explicit over implicit

## Important Context Placement
Critical information is placed at the END of rules (LLMs prioritize recent context).
